{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1503191-spirits-as-mentor-retainer-etc","id":1503191,"title":"Spirits as Mentor/Retainer/Etc","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-02-15T17:13:04-08:00","id":1503191,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Spirits as Mentor/Retainer/Etc","content":"Hello!<br /> <br /> So having read the rules for Ghoul Retainers, I wanted to see if there were any similar rules covering ephemeral entities as part of those social merits- or if using them unmodified is simply kosher.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4578-zale","name":"Zale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4578_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-18T15:09:54-08:00","id":1503401,"title":"","content":"The Retainer merit is very flexible although the ST should probably be mindful that it\u2019s balanced to be used as worded in the rules. A spirit as a cooperative NPC is too useful to allow unrestrained.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-18T15:28:26-08:00","id":1503403,"title":"","content":"Well, what is the reason for them to work as a Retainer ? Spirits are monomaniacal despite their level of intelligence, they have a predatory instinct as opposed to a human's pack instinct. Their power source and food is based on spreading the concepts they embody, they live in a society where a moment of weakness makes them a prize to be devoured by a rival or opportunist sycophant. Their morality revolves entirely over Essence and growing their concepts.<br /> <br /> Which means there has to be a reason for them to serve the character. Maybe a deal was struck with the ruler of their choir ? Maybe the character is promoting their agenda on the hopes of becoming a Purified ? Maybe one of their endeavors generates ample Essence for the spirit and something else for the character?<br /> <br /> Since money is likely not enough to bribe them, there needs to be a justification, which could come with according string attached. Rank 1 and 2 should be fairly easy to justify, like mutual defense while the spirit tries to grow. Rank 3 probably requires interests to align. Rank 4 and 5 require something major to justify, since at that point they are likely on the level of City Fathers or powerful enough to be considered natural disasters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-18T16:43:02-08:00","id":1503408,"title":"","content":"I'd honestly just modify the Familiar merit from Mage.<br /> <br /> For point-pool entites like Werewolves, it could probably be identical. Or the Werewolf's Essence pool is reduced by 1 for every Familiar, although that seems a bit too harsh for a relatively simple thing.<br /> <br /> For mortals, you could probably get by with a dot of Willpower that can't be accessed while the Familiar is maintained, or being inflicted with a Condition appropriate to the Entity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 02-18-2023, 07:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}